## Design direction

A custom sports medal starts with the event identity, award hierarchy and ribbon presentation, then resolves the artwork into a durable commemorative object.

For custom sports medals, begin with the part of the artwork that must read first. Keep the outline, smallest lettering, color breaks and functional details clear, then use finish and presentation to support the design rather than compete with it.

## Confirmed choices and project decisions

- Base materials include zinc alloy and iron.
- Back treatments include a standard sandblasted surface plus optional polished, laser-marked, or raised-back text treatments.
- Standard packaging is an OPP bag.

## Preparing your brief

Send the artwork, intended dimensions, quantity, delivery destination and required timing. Note which surfaces, moving parts, attachments or packaging details matter most so the quotation can be based on one clear specification.

Golden One will use the approved brief as the basis for the final product specification; unconfirmed materials, claims and performance details are not assumed.
